# Known-good matches for scripts/check-safety.sh.
#
# Format: one entry per line, "<path glob>|<fixed text>". A finding is
# dropped when its file path matches the glob (shell pattern, "*" also
# matches "/") and its line contains the fixed text. Keep each entry as
# narrow as possible and give the reason in a comment above it. Never add
# a real OIN, name, hostname or secret here: remove the value instead.

# ── Synthetic OINs with a real-looking prefix ────────────────────────────
# Real OINs start with 0000000 plus a register digit, so the check flags
# every such number. These are made-up test and demo values (sequences or
# repeated digits); none is a registered organisation.
*|00000001234567890000
*|00000009876543210000
*|00000005555555550000
*|00000004000000004000
*|00000003000000003000
*|00000001000000000001

# JSON-number parsing test: a 20-digit counting sequence, not an OIN.
services/ftv-graphql-mapper/mapper_test.go|"12345678901234567890"

# ── Test fixtures that look like secrets ─────────────────────────────────
# A plain-text marker the test checks is NOT returned; not a credential.
services/dev-portal-backend/main_test.go|const secret = "outside-policy-content"

# Connection-string parsing test with a dummy password "pw" for a host that
# only exists in the local Docker Compose network.
services/dev-portal-backend/adl_test.go|postgres://adl_reader:pw@postgres-ftv:5432
